#exception-box(title: "THE SEVEN FATAL CUET TRAPS")[
  1. *Trap 1 (UN Day vs India's Accession Date):* UN Day is celebrated on *24 October 1945*, but India signed the Charter on *30 October 1945*. Do not confuse these two dates!
  2. *Trap 2 (Location of the ICJ):* The International Court of Justice is seated in *The Hague, Netherlands*, NOT in New York or Geneva.
  3. *Trap 3 (Non-Permanent UNSC Term & Re-election):* Non-permanent members serve *two-year terms* and *cannot* be immediately re-elected.
  4. *Trap 4 (Trusteeship Council vs Human Rights Council):* The Trusteeship Council was *suspended in 1994*; the Human Rights Council was newly created in *2006* (replacing the Commission on Human Rights).
  5. *Trap 5 (WTO Founding Year):* The WTO was established on *1 January 1995* via the Marrakesh Agreement, NOT in 1948 (which was GATT) or 1991.
  6. *Trap 6 (IAEA Headquarters):* IAEA is headquartered in *Vienna, Austria*, NOT in Geneva or Paris.
  7. *Trap 7 (IMF Voting Power):* The IMF does NOT follow "one nation, one vote"; voting is quota-based, giving the US an effective unilateral veto (~16.5%).
]

